"""Build the ZenRay Meshes thumbnail: the V470 car, a radial vignette and the glowing title "Modeling Car".

1. The car: the composition function of EvolutionVideo.py places the four views on their flat background at the
   output size. The module is imported, not copied, so the thumbnail and the evolution video share one code path.
2. The title: a ZenRay Motion Design project copied from the end title is rendered by HyperFrames at one instant.
   Its size and centre are calibrated over a few passes until the ink width and the mass centre match the parameters.
3. The vignette and the final composite are computed in float and quantised with a small dither, so no band shows.
4. The outputs go to Out/, Index.md is rewritten, then Scripts/CheckThumbnail.py verifies the result.

Run it with the zenray-uv interpreter, from any folder:
  /Users/zenray/.venvs/zenray-uv/bin/python -I /Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-meshes/Montage/Thumbnail/Scripts/Thumbnail.py --help
"""

